# Defense-in-depth on top of the package.json "files" allowlist.
#
# "files" already whitelists exactly what ships (dist, ai, plugins assets, docs,
# README). This file is a second, subtractive guard: even if a future change
# loosens "files", test code, fixtures, coverage, and system cruft must never
# reach the published tarball. Keep it in sync with what is genuinely non-runtime.

# Test code and doubles
*.test.*
*.spec.*
__tests__/
__mocks__/
__snapshots__/
*.snap

# Fixtures and end-to-end scaffolding
fixtures/
**/fixtures/
e2e/
**/e2e/

# Coverage and build metadata
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.map

# Scratch / local working files
scratch/
*.local.*

# System / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
